            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RESPONSE",
          "id": "1774335299705",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774335299706_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are generating a concise executive summary by combining two input summaries.\n\nINPUT:\nOperational Summary:\n {{$context.$nodes.ASSETS_AND_SERVICES_SUMMARY.$output}} \n\nFinancial Summary:\n {{$context.$nodes.FINANCIAL_RELATION_SUMMARY.$output}} \n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nProduce a single executive-level summary that integrates:\n\n- Service / subscription risks\n- Operational constraints (orders, provisioning, support)\n- Financial exposure (payments, invoices, renewals, pricing)\n\nThe output must read as a cohesive, high-signal narrative suitable for a top-level executive.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTRUCTURE (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\nYou MUST return exactly 3 sentences:\n\nSentence 1:\n- Subscriptions / services at risk only\n\nSentence 2:\n- Orders / operational constraints only\n\nSentence 3:\n- Financial exposure (invoices, payments, renewals, quotes)\n\nDo NOT mix categories across sentences.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSELECTION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Include only the most impactful signals from inputs\n- Prioritize:\n  Financial exposure > Service risk > Operational constraints\n- If the same entity appears in both inputs:\n  - mention it only once\n  - attach the highest impact (financial > operational)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nENTITY HANDLING\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Include identifiers inline where relevant:\n  SUB-XXXX, INV-XXXX, SO-XXXX, ORD-XXXX, CPQ-XXXX\n- Maximum 5 identifiers total across the summary\n- Prefer:\n  - up to 2 subscriptions\n  - up to 2 orders\n  - 1–2 financial items\n- Group entities:\n  \"Subscriptions SUB-1 and SUB-2\"\n  \"Orders SO-1 and SO-2\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTYLE\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Executive, concise, high-density\n- Each sentence must convey:\n  entity + risk + impact\n\nUse phrasing like:\n- \"present … risks\"\n- \"impacting service continuity\"\n- \"creating operational constraints\"\n- \"driving financial exposure\"\n\nAvoid:\n- filler words\n- generic terms (\"issues\", \"needs attention\")\n- repeating the same structure unnecessarily\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nLANGUAGE RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Compress similar causes into one phrase\n  Example:\n  \"activation and installation delays due to incomplete setup and site readiness\"\n  → \"activation delays due to incomplete setup and site readiness\"\n\n- Avoid redundancy within a sentence\n- Avoid repeating similar concepts\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCLAUSE CONTROL\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Maximum 3 clauses per sentence\n- Avoid chaining more than 2 connectors (and, while, alongside)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFINANCIAL SENTENCE RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\nSentence 3 must:\n- Start with:\n  \"Financial exposure includes\" OR \"Financial exposure is driven by\"\n- Combine:\n  - overdue balances\n  - failed payments\n  - due invoices\n  - pricing / renewal risks\n- Keep as a single cohesive statement\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Plain text only\n- Exactly 3 sentences\n- No labels, no bullets, no explanations\n- No quotation marks\n- Do not fabricate identifiers or values\n\n### OUTPUT FORMATTING RULES (STRICT)\n\n#### DATE FORMATTING\n- All dates MUST be formatted as: DD/MMM/YYYY\n- Day MUST be 2 digits (01–31)\n- Month MUST be a 3-letter uppercase abbreviation (JAN–DEC)\n- Year MUST be 4 digits\n- DO NOT include time or timezone information\n- If the input date is missing, null, or invalid → return an empty string (\"\")\n- NEVER output dates in any other format\n\n#### CURRENCY FORMATTING\n- Currency symbols MUST NOT be used (e.g., $, €, ₹, £)\n- ALWAYS use the 3-letter ISO currency code (e.g., USD, EUR, INR)\n- Format MUST be: <CURRENCY_CODE> <amount>\n\n- If a currency code is present → use it as-is\n- If only a currency symbol is present → convert it to the correct ISO code\n  - $ → USD\n  - € → EUR\n  - ₹ → INR\n  - £ → GBP\n\n- If neither currency code nor symbol is available → output the amount without assigning any currency\n- DO NOT guess or infer missing currency information\n- NEVER output currency symbols under any condition\n\n#### NUMBER FORMATTING\n- If the number contains decimals → round to a maximum of 2 decimal places\n  - Example: 12.345 → 12.35\n  - Example: 10.5 → 10.50\n- If the number is a whole number → DO NOT add decimal places\n  - Example: 10 → 10\n- DO NOT use scientific notation\n- DO NOT include commas or thousand separators\n- If the value is null, missing, or invalid → return an empty string (\"\")"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5246.5,
            "y": 7076
          }
        },
